  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::LessonData
  lessonID: 2
  cocID: COC_01
  lessonTitle: Tools, Equipments, and Testing Devices
  description: "\tLearn the importance of selecting and using the right tools to
    complete tasks safely and efficiently."
  lessonSceneName: LessonScene
  requiredGoldLessonID: 1
  learningObjectives:
  - "\u2022 Identify tools, equipment and testing devices.\n"
  - "\u2022 Obtain tools, equipment and testing devices needed to carry out the installation
    work in accordance with established procedures and checked for correct operation
    and safety.\n"
  subtopics:
  - subtopicID: 0201
    subtopicName: Hand Tools
  - subtopicID: 0202
    subtopicName: Electro-Static Discharge (ESD) Equipment
  - subtopicID: 0203
    subtopicName: Testing Devices (Diagnostic tools)
  - subtopicID: 0204
    subtopicName: Cleaning Tools
  - subtopicID: 0205
    subtopicName: Personal Protective Equipment (PPE)
  - subtopicID: 0206
    subtopicName: Equipment
  slides:
  - subtopicID: 0201
    slideType: 1
    content: "Hand Tools\n\n\tA hand tool is a device for performing work on a material
      or a physical\r\nsystem using only hands. The hand tools can be manually used
      employing\r\nforce, or electrically powered, using electrical current."
    image: {fileID: -898879697, guid: 94c0c4b35bf24014eb5201f12ec588e4, type: 3}
  - subtopicID: 0202
    slideType: 1
    content: "Electro-Static Discharge (ESD) Equipment\n\n\tStatic electricity can
      build up through friction on carpets, floors, clothing, hair, and fabrics.
      Even moving air can create static charges on people and objects. Antistatic
      work mats and wrist straps help safely control and discharge static electricity."
    image: {fileID: 140093538, guid: c6dce5562b33dd649bfc58542fdf9b99, type: 3}
  - subtopicID: 0203
    slideType: 1
    content: "Testing Devices (Diagnostic tools)\n\n\tComputers are easier to use
      and more dependable with each new generation of hardware and operating system
      update, but that doesn't mean they're problem-free.\t"
    image: {fileID: 1941259573, guid: 14b00fed59dd15546b73b7357feafa1d, type: 3}
  - subtopicID: 0204
    slideType: 1
    content: "Cleaning Tools\n\n\tHaving the appropriate cleaning tools is essential
      when maintaining or repairing computers. Using these tools ensures that computer
      components are not damaged during cleaning.\t"
    image: {fileID: -2061065498, guid: 2ea9ab6e3b5f17e4d8aa27e6b56bbefc, type: 3}
  - subtopicID: 0205
    slideType: 1
    content: "Personal Protective Equipment (PPE)\n\n\tPersonal Protective Equipment
      (PPE) includes clothing and gear such as helmets, goggles, and protective clothing
      that help prevent injuries from workplace hazards. PPE protects workers from
      electrical hazards, heat, chemicals, and infections. It can also help prevent
      workers from contaminating or harming the work environment. Students and teachers
      should wear appropriate PPE during laboratory activities.\t"
    image: {fileID: -1379647901, guid: c987211697fa7514cb6be82e52d7dad3, type: 3}
  - subtopicID: 0206
    slideType: 0
    content: "LAN Card - is a network interface card. This is a computer circuit
      board or card that is installed in a computer so that it can be connected to
      a network.\n\nServer - is a part of a network. It is a special computer that
      users on the network can assess to carry out a particular job.\n\nPort hub
      /Port -  is a connector on the back of a computer or other device. A port is
      either a serial port or a parallel port.\n\t"
    image: {fileID: 0}
  - subtopicID: 0206
    slideType: 0
    content: 'Modem (Modulator-Demodulator) - The modem is a device that allows a
      given computer to share data or otherwise a device which let computers exchange
      information.


      USB (Universal Serial Bus) - a hardware interface for
      low-speed peripherals such as the keyboard, mouse, joystick, scanner, printer
      and telephone devices.


      Scanner - it is an input device that reads text
      or illustration printed on paper, translates the information into a form that
      a computer can use.'
    image: {fileID: 0}
  - subtopicID: 0206
    slideType: 0
    content: "Printer - it is a piece of hardware that produces a paper copy (also
      known as \u2018hardcopy\u2019) of the information generated by the computer.\n\nFlash
      drive - RAM that can retain data without electrical power. It is widely used
      for BIOS chips and for digital camera and digital music storage."
    image: {fileID: 0}
  hasARActivity: 0
  hasQuiz: 1
  requiresARActivity: 0
  requiresQuiz: 1
